## Negative findings (why this file is `.excluded`)

**ZERO verified public benchmark numbers were found for this exact model/ID.** Per the self-exclusion rule this file is saved as `GLM_5.3.md.excluded` — no scored `.md` is written, and no placeholder scores are invented.

What was verified (platform/catalog metadata only, no measured numbers):

- **Identity:** GPT-5.1 Codex Mini — OpenAI's fast, efficient small coding model, "optimized for quick code completion, simple refactoring, and routine programming tasks" (llm-stats vendor-blurb sourced from OpenAI's launch post).
- **Status:** live on the OpenCode Zen models endpoint (2026-10-17 scan: `gpt-5.1-codex-mini`, $0.25 in / $2.00 out per 1M, $0.025 cached read — Zen pricing table); **Zen deprecation table lists it as deprecated 2026-07-23** alongside the rest of the GPT-5.1 Codex line — deprecated but still served.
- **Specs (verified):** released 2025-11-12 (llm-stats); 400K in / 128K max output (llm-stats, matches the family); text + image in / text out (llm-stats); TTFT p95 1.00s, throughput p95 ~200 char/s (llm-stats, 7-day live traffic) — genuinely the fastest-tier Codex variant on latency.

Sources checked with no benchmark rows (2026-10-17):

- BenchLM (`gpt-5-1-codex-mini`): 404 — no page (the family list shows GPT-5.1 Codex at 50.37 but no Mini entry).
- Artificial Analysis: no Mini model page (AA measures the family under `gpt-5-1-codex` — none of its displayed rows are Mini-attributed).
- Vals AI (`openai_gpt-5.1-codex-mini`): 404 — no measured rows.
- llm-stats: full specs/pricing page but **zero benchmark rows** ("Quality Tracker" section empty).
- OpenAI GPT-5.1 launch post (openai.com/index/gpt-5-1/, fetched 2026-10-17): product/tone rollout coverage only — no Codex Mini eval table.

Interpolation from the GPT-5.1 Codex family (base 50.37 BenchLM) or from GPT-5.4 Mini positioning was deliberately NOT used — Mini is a distinct distillation with no published evals. A future re-research should look for (a) an OpenAI Codex Mini eval table or system card, (b) aggregator coverage (BenchLM/Vals/AA), (c) any post-deprecation archival snapshot — then write a fresh `GLM_5.3.md`.

Scores inside this file are intentionally omitted/ignored: the sync skips `.excluded` files loudly.

